    %% Simplified participants with student-friendly names
    participant You as "You"
    participant Program as "The Program"
    participant Grid as "The Grid"
    participant Rules as "The Rules"
    participant Screen as "The Screen"
    participant Buttons as "The Controls"

    %% Initial setup - simplified for students
    Note over Program: The program starts up
    Program->>Grid: Create an empty grid
    Grid-->>Program: Grid is ready
    Program->>Buttons: Create buttons and controls
    Buttons-->>Program: Controls are ready
    Program->>Grid: Fill with random cells
    Grid-->>Program: Random pattern created
    Program-->>Screen: Show the initial grid

    %% Main game loop explained simply
    Note over Program: Main Game Loop Begins

    loop Every time the screen refreshes
        Program->>Screen: Show generation count
        Program->>Screen: Draw the current grid
        Screen->>Grid: Get current cell states
        Grid-->>Screen: Here's what cells are alive/dead

        alt Game is running (Play button is active)
            Program->>Rules: Calculate the next generation
            Rules->>Grid: Read current grid
            Grid-->>Rules: Current cells data

            Note over Rules: Check each cell against Conway's rules
            Rules->>Grid: Update with new generation
            Grid-->>Rules: Grid updated

            Program->>Program: Count one more generation
        end
    end

    %% User interactions with simple explanations
    Note over You: Things You Can Do

    %% Play/Pause - student version
    You->>Buttons: Click Play/Pause
    Buttons->>Program: Start or stop the simulation
    Program->>Program: Change running state
    Program-->>Buttons: Update button appearance
    Buttons-->>You: Button changes to show new state

    %% Step
    You->>Buttons: Click Step Button
    Buttons->>Rules: Calculate just one step
    Rules->>Grid: Update grid one generation
    Grid-->>Screen: Show updated grid
    Screen-->>You: See one generation advance

    %% Clear
    You->>Buttons: Click Clear Button
    Buttons->>Grid: Remove all living cells
    Grid->>Grid: Set all cells to dead
    Grid-->>Screen: Show empty grid
    Screen-->>You: See empty grid

    %% Random
    You->>Buttons: Click Random Button
    Buttons->>Grid: Create random pattern
    Grid->>Grid: Randomly set some cells alive
    Grid-->>Screen: Show new random pattern
    Screen-->>You: See new random pattern

    %% Toggle cell
    You->>Screen: Click on a cell
    Screen->>Grid: Toggle this cell
    Grid->>Grid: Change cell (dead→alive or alive→dead)
    Grid-->>Screen: Update display
    Screen-->>You: See cell change state

    %% Speed - simplified
    You->>Buttons: Move speed slider
    Buttons->>Program: Change simulation speed
    Program-->>Screen: Run faster or slower
    Screen-->>You: See simulation speed change

    Note over Rules: Conway's Game of Life Rules:<br/>1. Any live cell with fewer than 2 live neighbors dies (loneliness)<br/>2. Any live cell with 2 or 3 live neighbors survives<br/>3. Any live cell with more than 3 neighbors dies (overcrowding)<br/>4. Any dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive (reproduction)

